//
// Llama-3.1-8B Q4NX DECODE compile-only smoke test: builds the fused_decode
// superkernel at the 8B geometry (MODEL_TYPE=LLAMA_3_1_8B) through the
// AIR -> AIE -> aiecc -> Peano pipeline. No NPU dispatch, no weight download.
//
// LBUILD=16 builds a tiny attention window: this gates that the 8B geometry
// lowers -- the split weight BOs (DECODE_WGROUP), the trimmed core stack
// (DECODE_STACK), and the vocab chunking -- not that it is fast. The production
// 2048 window is built by run_npu2_verify.lit / run_npu2_profile.lit.
//
// Collected by `check-programming-examples-llms-compile`, which filters on the path
// `llms/.*/run_npu2_compile` (not on a "peano" filename), like every other model.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, llvm_link_pre23
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_compile
// RUN: cd test_npu2_compile
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile compile-decode LBUILD=16 PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: 8B decode build complete
